title The free head and the honest lift agreed, and eight standing guards were found drifting behind their code
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds first, read one council-rota row, send each finished increment.
think Read KYRI and RADIANT_STYLE first, then REMEMBER, then the top three rows of session-logs/README.md. The running thread is the Caravan ladder lift arc; the newest recommend named bound_the_relay as the free head at 312.
think Standfast pass over crux/REDS.md first. An awk pass over every REDS %N heading found no row lacking a CLOSED counterpart -- 147 rows, every one closed. The constructive queue was therefore honestly open.
think Council rota row 2 -- Fire/Mars, cut and stop: Standfast, reds-first, the three depths of removal. Standfast named the shape of this lap before the lap knew it had one: stop the line the instant a red is real, find the root rather than the mark, resume on a witness on metal.
think Ran the fold queue rather than trusting the prior lap's row. bound_the_relay stood second by fall at 312 and first by price at widens=0, over seven rungs of a fifty-five-line body -- the narrowest and deepest row on the board.
think Hashed all eight bodies declaring the name before lifting. Seven identical; caravan/desist.rye differs in exactly one way, reaching walled, unbounded, and relayed off its report directly where the seven reach them through desist_of. That is the sub-record-accessor rule the arc has now stated four times, and it means the difference is meaning rather than drift.
think Seated the lifted body directly beneath hold_the_matter, since hold_the_matter consults exactly the walled count bound_the_relay writes. The seating is an argument, not an alphabetization.
think Carry fell 59,150 -> 58,838, a fall of 312 -- the scan's predicted number to the digit, twelve laps running. Lowered both ceilings together, the witness assert and the scan's CEILING default, which the suits_path lap learned the hard way.
think Then ran the choirs at a cold start rather than trusting them. Two reded, and the chain behind them ran eight witnesses deep.
obs REDS %147 is one root wearing four faces. The |+ barlus rune head entered glow/tokens.rye on 20260802 with the sumto folding gate, and the digraph count 27 stood written in six other places nobody brought along. brushstroke/brush_parse.rye grew ParseError from ten members to thirteen and BrushSurface from four fields to five while three pins held the old numbers. sunn8 grepped README.md for three literals a Radiant pass had reworded. sunn13 demanded all three licenses name a retired prior name.
obs The sunn13 case is the one worth carrying, and it is why a stale guard is worse than an absent one. Its RED said "LICENSE-MIT want Kaeden hold" -- pointing a repairing hand at the license rather than at the pin. A hand that obeyed it would have written a retired name back into a tree the identity sweep had deliberately cleared it from. A guard that has drifted does not merely fail to protect; it actively misdirects.
obs The repair for a missing rune is a name, not a number. |+ is seated as barlus -- | bar, + lus, the two-syllable rule every bar row above it keeps -- as the 28th G1 digraph row, so a reader who has met one bar row can pronounce this one unaided. Raising seven counts to 28 without naming the rune would have closed the witness and left the alphabet incomplete.
obs Brushstroke development stays paused; raising a pin so a meter describes the code it claims to describe is docs-implementation-sync, never feature work. No Brushstroke behavior moved.
obs The queue's new free head reads confer_words at 294 with widens=43, all of them import re-exports, beside reclaim_notes at the same fall over the same forty-three rungs costing nothing at all. Both are now asserted side by side, so a reader sees that free-by-the-priced-columns and free-absolutely are two different readings the meter keeps rather than one it collapses.
obs The dated-path census caught the new brief as a lost reference until it was staged, since the scan reads git ls-files rather than the working tree. Honest behavior, worth remembering: a new dated file is invisible to the census until it is tracked.
obs The Wayland-gated surface_study_choir stops at pond-frame on this pier for want of a display. That is the enclosure rather than a red, and it is named rather than counted as GREEN.
